    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `riskFlag` on the owner response\n\n`riskFlag` is `true` when **any** of three conditions holds, else `false`:\n1. the owner is a possible duplicate,\n2. its email domain is disposable-adjacent,\n3. its city is over its soft capacity.\n\nI reused the existing derived signals rather than recomputing them, keeping each responsibility in its own small unit:\n\n- **Possible duplicate** \u2014 already stored on the owner (`Owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`, set by `DetectPossibleDuplicate`).\n- **Over soft capacity** \u2014 reuses the existing per-city `capacityWarning` variable (`ResolveCapacityWarning`, the 40\u201349 band below the hard limit of 50), which already flows to both the create and read responders.\n- **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 a new, softer sibling of the existing disposable-domain rejection.\n\n### Where logic landed\n\n- **`DisposableDomains`** (new) \u2014 extracted the blocklist that was previously private inside `RejectDisposableEmail` into one shared home, with `isBlocked` (a known disposable domain \u2192 rejected outright) and `isAdjacent` (a subdomain of a blocked domain, e.g. `inbox.mailinator.com` \u2014 not blocked, but neighbouring one \u2192 risk). `RejectDisposableEmail` now delegates to it, so the two checks can't drift apart.\n- **`ResolveRiskFlag`** (new) + **`@RiskFlag`** qualifier \u2014 a single small step that composes the three signals and publishes the boolean, mirroring the existing `ResolveCapacityWarning`/`ResolveBulkSignupWarning` pattern.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `toOwnerDto(owner, bulkSignupWarning, capacityWarning, riskFlag)` overload layered on the existing ones.\n- **Responders** \u2014 `RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` now pass the flag through.\n- **Pipelines** \u2014 `resolveRiskFlag` wired into both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` after `resolveCapacityWarning`, so create and read responses agree.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 documented the new `riskFlag` field (the `OwnerDto` is generated from it).\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
